    (_voucher_step_carrierConvexOn_ambient_sublevel_nullMeasurable_29
      (E := E) (X := X) (φ := φ) hconv r).measurable_of_complete

/-- Finite-dimensional convex sets are Haar-null-measurable.

This is the Mathlib theorem that the previous reconstruction leaf was actually
able to justify. It is deliberately not upgraded to `MeasurableSet`: convexity
alone does not make an arbitrary finite-dimensional convex set Borel. For
example, an open Euclidean ball union an arbitrary subset of its sphere remains
convex, so a non-Borel boundary subset would give a non-Borel convex set. The
source-generated `Ψ` measurability route therefore needs a real regularity fact
for the paper's "simple" composite objective, not a false convex-set theorem. -/
private theorem _reconstruct_finiteDimensional_convex_nullMeasurableSet_41
    {C : Set E} (hC : Convex ℝ C) :
    NullMeasurableSet C (volume : Measure E) := by
  exact hC.nullMeasurableSet (volume : Measure E)

/-- Step-0 guard witness for the generated `Ψ` measurability boundary.

This is the formal shape of the obstruction behind the guarded
`theorem_4_4`: if a closed-carrier convex objective witness has a
nonmeasurable carrier restriction, then no theorem deriving carrier
measurability from only closedness plus `ConvexOn` can be sound. The
geometric source of such witnesses is the boundary-value phenomenon noted
above; the generated theorem therefore keeps `Measurable setup.PsiCarrier` as
an explicit local regularity premise instead of storing it in `Setup`. -/
private theorem _reconstruct_closed_carrier_convex_measurability_guard_needed_47
    {X : Set E} {φ : {x : E // x ∈ X} → ℝ}
    (hX_closed : IsClosed X)
    (hconv : ConvexOn ℝ X (SOptLib.totalizeOn X φ))
    (hnot_meas : ¬ Measurable φ) :
    ¬ (∀ {Y : Set E} {ψ : {x : E // x ∈ Y} → ℝ},
      IsClosed Y → ConvexOn ℝ Y (SOptLib.totalizeOn Y ψ) → Measurable ψ) := by
  intro hderive
  exact hnot_meas (hderive hX_closed hconv)

/-- Setup-level Step-0 obstruction for an unqualified carrier-measurability
derivation.

This specializes the previous generic obstruction to the actual AC-SA setup
record: if a fully formed setup has a nonmeasurable carrier objective, then no
uniform theorem can derive `Measurable setup.PsiCarrier` from the currently
stored source-facing setup fields alone. This does not construct such a setup;
it records the exact formal target a concrete countermodel must instantiate. -/
private theorem _reconstruct_theorem_4_4_unmeasurable_PsiCarrier_counterexample_48
    (badSetup : StochasticAcceleratedGradientDescentSetup E S)
    (hnot_meas : ¬ Measurable badSetup.PsiCarrier) :
    ¬ (∀ setup : StochasticAcceleratedGradientDescentSetup E S,
      Measurable setup.PsiCarrier) := by
  intro hderive
  exact hnot_meas (hderive badSetup)

