standalone prox-distance stability theorem, but that theorem was not a source
claim and is false with the fixed coefficients used there. A future proof should
derive the needed state regularity from the generated prox kernel's actual
measurability/growth properties or from a source-backed regularity theorem, not
from an unconditional `‖x* - x_t‖^2` estimate. -/
theorem generated_state_sq_integrable_from_prox_stability
    (execution : SourceGeneratedAcsExecution (E := E) (S := S) setup) :
    ∀ n : ℕ,
      Integrable
          (fun ω => ‖setup.xStar -
            (realization.generatedProcess execution n ω).x‖ ^ 2)
          realization.P ∧
        Integrable
          (fun ω => ‖setup.xStar -
            (realization.generatedProcess execution n ω).xBar‖ ^ 2)
          realization.P := by
  classical
  have hstab :
      ∀ t : {n : ℕ // 1 ≤ n},
        ∃ A B D C : ℝ,
          0 ≤ A ∧ 0 ≤ B ∧ 0 ≤ D ∧ 0 ≤ C ∧
          ∀ (prev : FeasibleStochasticAcceleratedGradientDescentState (E := E) setup.X)
            (ξ : S),
            ‖setup.xStar - execution.proxStepKernel t prev ξ‖ ^ 2 ≤
              A * ‖setup.xStar - prev.x‖ ^ 2 +
              B * ‖setup.xStar - prev.xBar‖ ^ 2 +
